From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:15:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Gap-fill by UID, per-target log filter, MCP permissions
 in the role editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Gap-fill: with an unchanged UIDVALIDITY the UIDs not archived in the
  folder are downloaded right away, without the header scan (Yandex answers
  each HEADER.FIELDS batch in seconds: hours per folder, sessions stuck with
  folders "pending"). A changed UIDVALIDITY keeps the header comparison.
  Logs the plan per folder at warn ("Gap-fill: plan").
- BICHON_LOG_FILTER (logger/filter.rs): RUST_LOG-style per-target levels,
  e.g. info,poem_mcpserver=warn — sync progress visible, mail bodies from
  the MCP library not logged. Falls back to BICHON_LOG_LEVEL.
- Web UI: account:sync and data:draft in the account role permission
  matrix (all three permission dialogs), en/ru labels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
